[
  {
    "comment_id": 4439238517,
    "path": "packages/infra-db/src/migrations/meta/_journal.json",
    "line": 9,
    "finding": "👮 **Wachiman** · 🟡🐛 **Consider · bug: Journal lists migrations 0000–0002 whose SQL files and snapshots are not in the tree**\n\nThis new journal lists `0000_baseline`, `0001_integrity` and `0002_account_provider_unique`. None of those `.sql` files or their `meta/000N_snapshot.json` files exist in `packages/infra-db/src/migrations/`: only the `0003` SQL and snapshot are there. The spec (`specs/2026-10-29-several-workspaces-design.md:1112-1118`) explains why: the chain belongs to PR #364, which has not merged. Until it does, `main` has a migrations folder whose journal points at missing files. `bun run db:migrate` (`drizzle-kit migrate`, `packages/infra-db/package.json:24`) would fail as soon as it tries to read `0000_baseline.sql`. The command is documented as unused today (`commands.md:33`), but it is still wired up. One option is to commit only the `0003` SQL and keep the journal out of this PR, so #364 brings the journal. Another is to land this after #364, so the folder never sits in a half-state on `main`.\n\n<!-- wachi:finding -->",
    "replies": [
      {
        "author": "csdev19",
        "body": "Declined, on purpose. Leaving the journal out is the riskier option. A migration file with its snapshot but no journal entry is silent: `drizzle-kit generate` (and #364's `db:check`) would treat `0003_snapshot.json` as the latest state and report no drift, while `db:migrate` would never apply `0003`. With the four-entry journal, each mismatch is loud. On `main` before #364, `db:migrate` fails at once on the missing `0000_baseline.sql` (and `commands.md` says not to use it yet). When both have merged, git reports an add/add conflict on `_journal.json`, resolved by taking the four-entry version. This PR is the top of a four-level stack, so in practice #364 lands first. The PR body and the spec (Cloud: server and client, \"Migration file\") record the merge rule."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "comment_id": 4439238524,
    "path": "packages/infra-db/src/migrations/meta/0003_snapshot.json",
    "line": 3,
    "finding": "👮 **Wachiman** · 🟡❓ **Consider · question: Snapshot chain points to a snapshot that isn't on main**\n\nThis snapshot's `prevId` (`86ab3674-…`) points to a `0002` snapshot that exists only in PR #364. In this checkout, `src/migrations/` holds just `0003_cloud_asset_workspace_id.sql`, `meta/0003_snapshot.json` and `meta/_journal.json`. The journal still lists `0000_baseline`, `0001_integrity` and `0002_account_provider_unique` (`_journal.json:9-23`), but none of their SQL files or snapshots are here.\n\nThe spec explains this (`specs/2026-10-29-several-workspaces-design.md:1112-1118`), and `commands.md:32-33` says `db:migrate` and `db:generate` aren't used yet. Until #364 merges, though, main ships a migrations folder that is broken: `bun run db:migrate` would fail looking for `0000_baseline.sql`, and the chain `drizzle-kit check` validates starts from a missing parent.\n\nCould this snapshot and the journal wait for #364, or land on top of it? Then main would carry the column only through `db:push`, which is how the spec says it ships today. If both PRs are definitely merging together, please confirm that this snapshot was generated from #364's exact `0002` snapshot. If #364's snapshot changes before it merges, the `prevId` here will no longer match.\n\n<!-- wachi:finding -->",
    "replies": [
      {
        "author": "csdev19",
        "body": "Confirmed: `0003_snapshot.json` was generated by `drizzle-kit generate` from a copy of #364's `packages/infra-db` at its current head, `0002_snapshot.json` included, plus only the one column. So `prevId` is that snapshot's id. If #364 regenerates `0002` before it merges, `0003` has to be regenerated on top of it. Holding the snapshot and journal back is declined, for the reason in the journal thread: a snapshot or SQL file without its journal entry makes `db:check` pass while `db:migrate` skips the column. The column still ships with `db:push` until #364 lands, as the spec says."
      }
    ]
  }
]

